{"type":"text","timestamp":1792509441094,"sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","part":{"id":"prt_159e37146001VimziLXY3MMq0y","messageID":"msg_159e2bf22001zsDoFp8YPWmHnN","sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","type":"text","text":"\n\nCheck 1 passes with `work_ratio` 0.395. My fast LexBFS is already 2.5x cheaper than the offline baseline. Now the goal is to avoid recomputing after updates. Let me first measure how often the old ordering survives a single edge flip, to know if a \"keep-if-valid\" strategy pays off.\n\n","time":{"start":1792509440326,"end":1792509441079}}}
