{"type":"text","timestamp":1792509613980,"sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","part":{"id":"prt_159e5f7ff001L50r36Y50fWurV","messageID":"msg_159e45901001hH699RFAAIqbvs","sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","type":"text","text":"\n\nCheck 1 passes at `work_ratio` 0.395. Now the goal is to avoid full recomputes after updates. My measurement showed 76.6% of single flips keep the old ordering valid, but a full (LB) check costs ~2.6x a recompute. The key is a *focused* check: after flipping edge (u,v), only triples where a, b, or c is in {u,v} can change (LB) status, so I can check those in O(n²) using a maintained `minD` witness table. Let me implement that as check 2 and measure whether it actually beats the fast recompute.\n\n","time":{"start":1792509605887,"end":1792509613970}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792509614024,"sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-95c22e21707ef3cf","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Dynamic algorithm candidate. Edit this file; keep the three functions.\n\nStrategy: keep the old LexBFS ordering after an update when it is still valid,\nand only recompute from scratch when a single edge flip actually breaks the\n(LB) 4-point property. After flipping edge (u, v), only triples (a, b, c) with\nat least one of a, b, c in {u, v} can change (LB) status (the flip touches\nonly edges incident to u or v, and for triples with a, b, c all outside\n{u, v} neither the antecedent nor any witness edge changes). So validity is\ncertified by checking exactly those affected triples, in O(n^2), using a\nmaintained minD[b][c] = earliest (in the ordering) vertex d that is a\nneighbour of b and a non-neighbour of c. minD changes only for pairs with b\nor c in {u, v}, so it is updated incrementally in O(n^2) per flip.\n\"\"\"\n\nINF = 10 ** 9\n\n\ndef _lexbfs(graph):\n    \"\"\"Partition-refinement LexBFS (Habib-McConnell-Paul-Viennot).\n\n    Starts at vertex 0 with the minimum-id tie-break. Returns a valid\n    LexBFS ordering of the undirected graph given as a 0/1 adjacency matrix.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(graph)\n    Pi = [list(range(n))]\n    order = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        p = Pi[0][0]\n        order.append(p)\n        if len(Pi[0]) == 1:\n            Pi = Pi[1:]\n        else:\n            Pi[0] = Pi[0][1:]\n        row = graph[p]\n        newPi = []\n        for C in Pi:\n            a = [v for v in C if row[v]]\n            b = [v for v in C if not row[v]]\n            if a:\n                newPi.append(a)\n            if b:\n                newPi.append(b)\n        Pi = newPi\n    return order\n\n\ndef _mind_pair(graph, pos, n, b, c):\n    \"\"\"Earliest (in `pos`) vertex d that is a neighbour of b and a\n    non-neighbour of c, or INF if none. This is the witness for the (LB)\n    consequent of any triple whose later two vertices are (b, c).\"\"\"\n    if b == c:\n        return INF\n    best = INF\n    for d in range(n):\n        if d != b and d != c and graph[b][d] and not graph[c][d]:\n            pd = pos[d]\n            if pd < best:\n                best = pd\n    return best\n\n\ndef _mind_all(graph, pos, n):\n    return [[_mind_pair(graph, pos, n, b, c) for c in range(n)] for b in range(n)]\n\n\ndef _pos_of(ordering):\n    pos = [0] * len(ordering)\n    for i, v in enumerate(ordering):\n        pos[v] = i\n    return pos\n\n\ndef _focused_valid(graph, pos, minD, n, u, v):\n    \"\"\"Check (LB) for every triple (a, b, c) with pos a < b < c and at least\n    one of a, b, c in {u, v}. Triples with all three outside {u, v} are\n    unaffected by the flip, so they need not be checked.\"\"\"\n    for a in (u, v):\n        pa = pos[a]\n        for b in range(n):\n            if b == a:\n                continue\n            pb = pos[b]\n            if pb <= pa:\n                continue\n            gab = graph[a][b]\n            for c in range(n):\n                if c == a or c == b:\n                    continue\n                pc = pos[c]\n                if pc <= pb:\n                    continue\n                if graph[a][c] and not gab:\n                    if minD[b][c] >= pa:\n                        return False\n    for b in (u, v):\n        pb = pos[b]\n        for a in range(n):\n            if a == b:\n                continue\n            pa = pos[a]\n            if pa >= pb:\n                continue\n            gab = graph[a][b]\n            for c in range(n):\n                if c == a or c == b:\n                    continue\n                pc = pos[c]\n                if pc <= pb:\n                    continue\n                if graph[a][c] and not gab:\n                    if minD[b][c] >= pa:\n                        return False\n    for c in (u, v):\n        pc = pos[c]\n        for a in range(n):\n            if a == c:\n                continue\n            pa = pos[a]\n            for b in range(n):\n                if b == a or b == c:\n                    continue\n                pb = pos[b]\n                if pb <= pa or pb >= pc:\n                    continue\n                if graph[a][c] and not graph[a][b]:\n                    if minD[b][c] >= pa:\n                        return False\n    return True\n\n\ndef _rebuild(graph):\n    n = len(graph)\n    ordering = _lexbfs(graph)\n    pos = _pos_of(ordering)\n    minD = _mind_all(graph, pos, n)\n    return {\"ordering\": ordering, \"pos\": pos, \"minD\": minD, \"n\": n}\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    return _rebuild(graph)\n\n\ndef _update(graph, edge, state):\n    n = state[\"n\"]\n    u, v = edge\n    pos = state[\"pos\"]\n    minD = [row[:] for row in state[\"minD\"]]\n    # Only pairs with b or c in {u, v} change; recompute those.\n    for b in (u, v):\n        for c in range(n):\n            if c != b:\n                minD[b][c] = _mind_pair(graph, pos, n, b, c)\n    for c in (u, v):\n        for b in range(n):\n            if b != c:\n                minD[b][c] = _mind_pair(graph, pos, n, b, c)\n    if _focused_valid(graph, pos, minD, n, u, v):\n        return {\"ordering\": state[\"ordering\"], \"pos\": pos, \"minD\": minD, \"n\": n}\n    return _rebuild(graph)\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    return _update(graph, edge, state)\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    return _update(graph, edge, state)\n","filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s2/candidate.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s2/candidate.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s2/candidate.py","time":{"start":1792509613950,"end":1792509614016}},"id":"prt_159e5fadc001X6zwuk36hACW8x","sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","messageID":"msg_159e45901001hH699RFAAIqbvs"}}
