{"type":"text","timestamp":1792509702691,"sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","part":{"id":"prt_159e761da001IFNF9vhEM94pqA","messageID":"msg_159e7087b001sW6L7fX0GU5L8B","sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","type":"text","text":"\n\nCheck 2 (keep-if-valid) is worse: `work_ratio` 1.66 vs check 1's 0.395. The keep-path check is ~4x more expensive than the fast recompute, so \"avoid recompute\" loses. The benchmark confirms single-pass LexBFS is the fastest recompute (~1.5x faster than my check-1 version). Let me use it with always-recompute as check 3.\n\n","time":{"start":1792509698522,"end":1792509702685}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792509702740,"sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-acc8fc9fae21b6d7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Dynamic algorithm candidate. Edit this file; keep the three functions.\n\nStrategy: recompute a valid LexBFS ordering from scratch after every update,\nusing the fastest correct partition-refinement LexBFS (single pass per cell,\nno per-step neighbour set). A keep-if-valid variant was measured to cost more\nthan this recompute (the (LB) validity check is O(n^2) with a larger constant\nthan the recompute), so the fastest recompute minimises work_ratio.\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _lexbfs(graph):\n    \"\"\"Partition-refinement LexBFS (Habib-McConnell-Paul-Viennot).\n\n    Starts at vertex 0 with the minimum-id tie-break. Returns a valid\n    LexBFS ordering of the undirected graph given as a 0/1 adjacency matrix.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(graph)\n    Pi = [list(range(n))]\n    order = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        p = Pi[0][0]\n        order.append(p)\n        if len(Pi[0]) == 1:\n            Pi = Pi[1:]\n        else:\n            Pi[0] = Pi[0][1:]\n        row = graph[p]\n        newPi = []\n        for C in Pi:\n            a = []\n            b = []\n            for v in C:\n                if row[v]:\n                    a.append(v)\n                else:\n                    b.append(v)\n            if a:\n                newPi.append(a)\n            if b:\n                newPi.append(b)\n        Pi = newPi\n    return order\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(graph)}\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(graph)}\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(graph)}\n","filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s2/candidate.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s2/candidate.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s2/candidate.py","time":{"start":1792509702673,"end":1792509702730}},"id":"prt_159e76548001g0S6PJhfWgmmyn","sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","messageID":"msg_159e7087b001sW6L7fX0GU5L8B"}}
