{"type":"text","timestamp":1792509794190,"sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","part":{"id":"prt_159e8c87b001CINz486WU1003m","messageID":"msg_159e8693f001ayceIDWfI0gbH6","sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","type":"text","text":"\n\nThe fixed bitmask-label LexBFS is valid (0 invalid in 30000 trials, including n=6) and consistently faster than single-pass (0.64x at n=2, ~0.9x at n=3-5). Let me test it as a candidate to get the real `work_ratio`.\n\n","time":{"start":1792509790331,"end":1792509794185}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792509794231,"sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-858b48cdb58e1fa1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Dynamic algorithm candidate. Edit this file; keep the three functions.\n\nStrategy: recompute a valid LexBFS ordering from scratch after every update,\nusing a bitmask-label LexBFS. label[u] is the bitstring of u's non-adjacencies\nto the already-ordered vertices, with position 0 (the first selected vertex)\nas the most significant bit, so the numeric minimum of (label, id) is exactly\nthe lexicographically-smallest LexBFS choice (neighbours preferred, id\ntie-break). Each step is O(n) integer bit-ops, so the whole search is O(n^2)\nwith a small constant and no per-step list allocation.\n\nA keep-if-valid variant was measured to cost more than this recompute (the\n(LB) validity check has a larger constant than the recompute), so the fastest\nrecompute minimises work_ratio.\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _lexbfs(graph):\n    \"\"\"Bitmask-label LexBFS. Returns a valid LexBFS ordering of the undirected\n    graph given as a 0/1 adjacency matrix (start 0, min-id tie-break).\"\"\"\n    n = len(graph)\n    label = [0] * n\n    unvisited = list(range(n))\n    order = []\n    for step in range(n):\n        best = -1\n        best_label = -1\n        for u in unvisited:\n            lu = label[u]\n            if best < 0 or lu < best_label or (lu == best_label and u < best):\n                best = u\n                best_label = lu\n        order.append(best)\n        unvisited.remove(best)\n        row = graph[best]\n        bit = 1 << (n - 1 - step)  # position 0 = MSB -> numeric == lexicographic\n        for u in unvisited:\n            if not row[u]:\n                label[u] |= bit\n    return order\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(graph)}\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(graph)}\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(graph)}\n","filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s2/candidate.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s2/candidate.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s2/candidate.py","time":{"start":1792509794175,"end":1792509794224}},"id":"prt_159e8ca0b001dE41bZy4xS7H76","sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","messageID":"msg_159e8693f001ayceIDWfI0gbH6"}}
