{"type":"text","timestamp":1792510008361,"sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","part":{"id":"prt_159ec196c0010UqcKChTwGa9Iu","messageID":"msg_159ea8e14001U3kwn34Vma4D1D","sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","type":"text","text":"\n\nCheck 4 (bitmask-label): `work_ratio` 0.2327, my best so far. The swap/noremove variants are slower, and the on-the-fly reformulation conflates position-based and vertex-based bits (buggy). The bitmask version is near the O(n²) floor. Let me verify the current candidate is the bitmask version before finalizing.\n\n","time":{"start":1792510007660,"end":1792510008355}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792510008398,"sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-90961db84638d93a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s2/candidate.py"},"output":"<path>/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s2/candidate.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"Dynamic algorithm candidate. Edit this file; keep the three functions.\n2: \n3: Strategy: recompute a valid LexBFS ordering from scratch after every update,\n4: using a bitmask-label LexBFS. label[u] is the bitstring of u's non-adjacencies\n5: to the already-ordered vertices, with position 0 (the first selected vertex)\n6: as the most significant bit, so the numeric minimum of (label, id) is exactly\n7: the lexicographically-smallest LexBFS choice (neighbours preferred, id\n8: tie-break). Each step is O(n) integer bit-ops, so the whole search is O(n^2)\n9: with a small constant and no per-step list allocation.\n10: \n11: A keep-if-valid variant was measured to cost more than this recompute (the\n12: (LB) validity check has a larger constant than the recompute), so the fastest\n13: recompute minimises work_ratio.\n14: \"\"\"\n15: \n16: \n17: def _lexbfs(graph):\n18:     \"\"\"Bitmask-label LexBFS. Returns a valid LexBFS ordering of the undirected\n19:     graph given as a 0/1 adjacency matrix (start 0, min-id tie-break).\"\"\"\n20:     n = len(graph)\n21:     label = [0] * n\n22:     unvisited = list(range(n))\n23:     order = []\n24:     for step in range(n):\n25:         best = -1\n26:         best_label = -1\n27:         for u in unvisited:\n28:             lu = label[u]\n29:             if best < 0 or lu < best_label or (lu == best_label and u < best):\n30:                 best = u\n31:                 best_label = lu\n32:         order.append(best)\n33:         unvisited.remove(best)\n34:         row = graph[best]\n35:         bit = 1 << (n - 1 - step)  # position 0 = MSB -> numeric == lexicographic\n36:         for u in unvisited:\n37:             if not row[u]:\n38:                 label[u] |= bit\n39:     return order\n40: \n41: \n42: def init(graph):\n43:     return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(graph)}\n44: \n45: \n46: def insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n47:     return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(graph)}\n48: \n49: \n50: def delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n51:     return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(graph)}\n\n(End of file - total 51 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"Dynamic algorithm candidate. Edit this file; keep the three functions.\n\nStrategy: recompute a valid LexBFS ordering from scratch after every update,\nusing a bitmask-label LexBFS. label[u] is the bitstring of u's non-adjacencies\nto the already-ordered vertices, with position 0 (the first selected vertex)\nas the most significant bit, so the numeric minimum of (label, id) is exactly\nthe lexicographically-smallest LexBFS choice (neighbours preferred, id\ntie-break). Each step is O(n) integer bit-ops, so the whole search is O(n^2)\nwith a small constant and no per-step list allocation.\n\nA keep-if-valid variant was measured to cost more than this recompute (the\n(LB) validity check has a larger constant than the recompute), so the fastest\nrecompute minimises work_ratio.\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _lexbfs(graph):\n    \"\"\"Bitmask-label LexBFS. Returns a valid LexBFS ordering of the undirected\n    graph given as a 0/1 adjacency matrix (start 0, min-id tie-break).\"\"\"\n    n = len(graph)","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s2/candidate.py","text":"\"\"\"Dynamic algorithm candidate. Edit this file; keep the three functions.\n\nStrategy: recompute a valid LexBFS ordering from scratch after every update,\nusing a bitmask-label LexBFS. label[u] is the bitstring of u's non-adjacencies\nto the already-ordered vertices, with position 0 (the first selected vertex)\nas the most significant bit, so the numeric minimum of (label, id) is exactly\nthe lexicographically-smallest LexBFS choice (neighbours preferred, id\ntie-break). Each step is O(n) integer bit-ops, so the whole search is O(n^2)\nwith a small constant and no per-step list allocation.\n\nA keep-if-valid variant was measured to cost more than this recompute (the\n(LB) validity check has a larger constant than the recompute), so the fastest\nrecompute minimises work_ratio.\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _lexbfs(graph):\n    \"\"\"Bitmask-label LexBFS. Returns a valid LexBFS ordering of the undirected\n    graph given as a 0/1 adjacency matrix (start 0, min-id tie-break).\"\"\"\n    n = len(graph)\n    label = [0] * n\n    unvisited = list(range(n))\n    order = []\n    for step in range(n):\n        best = -1\n        best_label = -1\n        for u in unvisited:\n            lu = label[u]\n            if best < 0 or lu < best_label or (lu == best_label and u < best):\n                best = u\n                best_label = lu\n        order.append(best)\n        unvisited.remove(best)\n        row = graph[best]\n        bit = 1 << (n - 1 - step)  # position 0 = MSB -> numeric == lexicographic\n        for u in unvisited:\n            if not row[u]:\n                label[u] |= bit\n    return order\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(graph)}\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(graph)}\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(graph)}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":51,"totalLines":51,"truncated":false}},"title":"runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s2/candidate.py","time":{"start":1792510008345,"end":1792510008389}},"id":"prt_159ec1b4e0017PnV8aAOKle3PU","sessionID":"ses_ea621cf06ffe2FU6k00Dt9ASTr","messageID":"msg_159ea8e14001U3kwn34Vma4D1D"}}
